I exported TAU/clamp from audio unnecessarily; fine, but game can define its own.

Now game.js — the meat. Need to carefully implement. Let's design class and functions.

World radius 400.

Input object provided by main, with fields:
```js
this.input = { moveX:0, moveY:0, aimAngle:-Math.PI/2, fire:false, slow:false, dashPressed:false, touch:false };
```

Game callbacks:
```js
this.onSfx = () => {};
this.onToast = () => {};
this.onBanner = () => {};
```
Set by main.

Methods:
- reset()
- update(dt)
- helpers ...
- debug API maybe methods spawnBoss, etc.

Pseudo-random: Math.random fine.

Details:

**reset**
```js
reset() {
 this.status='playing';
 this.timeScale=1; this.slowTarget=1; this.input.slow=false; this.input.fire=false; this.input.dashPressed=false;
 this.realT=0; this.elapsed=0; this.wave=1; this.waveT=0; this.waveDuration=16;
 this.score=0; this.combo=0; this.comboT=0; this.stolen=0; this.debtFrac=0; this.debt=[]; this.moteSeq=0;
 this.enemies=[]; this.bullets=[]; this.particles=[]; this.rings=[]; this.texts=[]; this.pickups=[]; this.echoBuffer=[];
 this.player={...};
 this.shake=0; this.flash=0; this.hitstop=0; this.overdrive=0; this.boss=null; this.bossSeq=0;
 this.spawnT=1.0; this.lastCollectorSpawn=-999; this.overdueNotified=false;
 this.stats={kills:0,collectors:0,collectorsFaced:0,borrowed:0,wave:1,score:0,time:0};
 this.flags={...};
 this.spawnInitial();
 this.onBanner? Need wave 1 banner at t=0.6 maybe. Set event queue.
}
```
Better `bannerTimer`/event? Call `onBanner` at reset? Overlay just hidden; banner can show. But startGame hides title and game starts; banner "WAVE 01 — THE PRESENT" might appear. Fine. Call `onBanner("WAVE 01","THE PRESENT RESISTS")` after tiny delay? Could just call immediately. UI banner animation. Let's do at reset (main starts game after overlay click), banner visible under overlay fade. Good.

Actually `onBanner` callbacks must be set before reset; main sets before start game. Yes.

Initial enemies: 3 husks at angles -π/2, π/6, 5π/6? Player center. radius ~330. SpawnT 0.6. They immediately approach.

**update(dtReal)**

```js
update(dtRaw) {
  const dt = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dtRaw));
  this.realT += dt;
  // decay shake, flash even outside playing
  this.updateGlobalFx(dt);
  if (this.status === 'playing') {
     this.elapsed += dt;
     this.updateTime(dt);
     this.updatePlayer(dt);
     this.updateDebt(dt);
     this.updateWaves(dt);
     if (this.hitstop > 0) { this.hitstop -= dt; /* still update particles? */ }
     const worldDt = dt * this.timeScale;
     this.updateEnemies(worldDt, dt);
     this.updateBoss(worldDt, dt);
     this.updateBullets(dt);
     this.updatePickups(dt);
     this.collide();
     this.updateEffects(dt);
     this.updateCombo(dt);
  } else if (this.status === 'dying') {
     this.timeScale += (0.22 - this.timeScale) * min(1, dt*4);
     this.updateEnemies(dt*this.timeScale, dt);
     this.updateBullets(dt); // bullets slowed by time; use *timeScale for hostile
     this.updateEffects(dt);
     this.deathT -= dt;
     if (this.deathT <= 0) { this.status='dead'; this.stats.time=this.elapsed; }
  } else if (this.status === 'victory') {
     ...
  }
}
```

Player bullets update with dtReal; hostile with dtReal*timeScale. In updateBullets(dt) use `bullet.friendly ? dt : dt*this.timeScale`. But during dying timeScale lower; fine. Hit detection still, but skip damage if dying.

Time:
```js
const active = this.status==='playing' && this.input.slow && this.input.fire !== undefined; // just slow
this.slowTarget = active ? 0.19 : 1;
const rate = active ? 12 : 7;
this.timeScale += (target-ts)*min(1,rate*dt);
if (active) {
  this.stolen += dt;
  this.debtFrac += dt;
  while (debtFrac >= 1) { debtFrac -= 1; this.addDebt(); }
}
this.overdrive += ((this.timeScale < 0.55 ? 1 : 0) - this.overdrive)*min(1,10*dt);
this.stats.borrowed = this.stolen; // continuous
```
Call audio.setSlow? Main can detect `game.timeScale < 0.5` each frame and call audio.setSlow, once. Or game calls `this.onSlowChange(active)` callback. Add `this.slowActive` bool and `onEvent('slow', active)`. Main handles audio. In updateTime:
```js
const slowed = this.timeScale < 0.55;
if (slowed !== this.wasSlowed) { this.wasSlowed=slowed; this.onSlow?.(slowed); }
```
Use callback `this.onSlowChange`.

Debt:
```js
addDebt() {
  this.debt.push({id: ++this.moteSeq, fuse: DEBT_FUSE});
