If no space and ready exists, caption UI; notification once per few seconds: `if (!overdueNotified) toast('FUTURE QUEUED · TOO MANY COLLECTORS', 'warn')`. Reset when space. Keep.

But debt motes count activeCollectors maxed at 4 → debt can grow unbounded; cap debt pending at 18; if exceeds, force spawn even over cap? Could cause death; but holding slow for 20s is suicide anyway. Let's cap queue at 24 and set toast. Performance okay. Perhaps if debt > 20, player takes 1 damage/sec "interest". Overkill. Add "DEBT SATURATED" and force fuse 0; max collectors cap 5. Not needed.

