content.text:
Collector fire block:

```js
if (enemy.fireT <= 0 && enemy.telegraph <= 0) { start }
if (enemy.telegraph > 0 && enemy.telegraph <= 0.02) { fire }
```
Change second to telegraphEnded. But if telegraph ended this frame, then at start of collector block after decrement, `enemy.telegraph` is 0; the first condition `fireT <=0 && telegraph <=0` — fireT was not reset yet (it's <=0 because it triggered the telegraph earlier), so it would start a new telegraph in the same frame before firing, then telegraphedEnded fires anyway and resets fireT. Order currently: telegraph start check then fire check. With ended, it would start a new telegraph then fire and set fireT, then telegraph=0. No lasting bug, but avoid by check ended first. Reorder: do fire if ended else if fireT<=0 && telegraph<=0 start. Let's replace.

