content.text:
Now bake vignette + grain into buildBackdropCache after stars/dust/horizon lines. Careful order: backdrop cache currently: bg gradient, nebula, lift, stars, dust, horizon lines. Add vignette after all. Grain last.

Vignette in cache: emulate CSS:
- radial ellipse: center (w/2, h*0.48), extents 0.78w x 0.72h? CSS `ellipse 78% 72%` means rx=78% of width? Actually for background radial-gradient, percentages refer to box dimensions: 78% of width? For ellipse, rx=78% of width? Hmm CSS defines horizontal radius as percentage of width and vertical of height, so rx=0.78w (very large) and ry=0.72h. Stops: transparent 38%, 0.42 at 72%, 0.88 at 100%.
- linear gradient top rgba(0,2,6,0.45) at 0 → transparent 12%, transparent 86% → rgba(0,2,6,0.55) at 100%.

Use ctx.save(); translate(w/2,h/2); scale(1, (0.72*h)/(0.78*w))? Simpler draw radial gradient with radius r = max(w,h)*0.8 and stops adjusted, plus linear top/bottom.

I'll implement:
```js
const vig = ctx.createRadialGradient(w/2, h*0.48, Math.min(w,h)*0.28, w/2, h*0.48, Math.max(w,h)*0.72);
vig.addColorStop(0, "rgba(0,2,6,0)");
vig.addColorStop(0.55, "rgba(0,2,6,0.18)");
vig.addColorStop(1, "rgba(0,2,6,0.62)");
ctx.fillStyle = vig; ctx.fillRect(0,0,w,h);
const topBottom = ctx.createLinearGradient(0,0,0,h);
topBottom.addColorStop(0,"rgba(0,2,6,0.42)");
topBottom.addColorStop(0.12,"rgba(0,2,6,0)");
topBottom.addColorStop(0.86,"rgba(0,2,6,0)");
topBottom.addColorStop(1,"rgba(0,2,6,0.5)");
ctx.fillStyle=topBottom; ctx.fillRect(0,0,w,h);
```

Grain: draw 1px lines every 3px with 0.02 white and every 4px vertical 0.008. In cache once. Use fillStyle and fillRect loops (300+360 rects one time). Could use line path strokes: beginPath for all horizontal lines then stroke once. Much faster. 

```js
ctx.save();
ctx.strokeStyle="rgba(255,255,255,0.022)";
ctx.lineWidth=1;
ctx.beginPath();
for(let y=0;y<h;y+=3){ctx.moveTo(0,y+0.5);ctx.lineTo(w,y+0.5);}
ctx.stroke();
ctx.strokeStyle="rgba(255,255,255,0.01)";
ctx.beginPath();
for(let x=0;x<w;x+=4){ctx.moveTo(x+0.5,0);ctx.lineTo(x+0.5,h);}
ctx.stroke();
ctx.restore();
```

Note backdrop cache covers whole screen; the arena is drawn on top, so vignette/grain won't darken the arena interior and HUD. CSS vignette used to be above everything (z 40) including arena & HUD, giving strong mood. Baked version under arena only affects outer edges (arena at center mostly unaffected). That might actually be visually fine or even better (arena readable). But the vignette edges where the arena rim is near screen edges could darken rim slightly, good.

However the title screen overlay is DOM; fine.

Let me add.

